      "Singapore shoppers are experienced online buyers. They compare prices across your site, Shopee, Lazada and Amazon.sg in the same minute, expect a checkout that works on a phone without friction, and assume delivery within a day or two because the whole country is small. A store that looks dated, loads slowly or hides the delivery fee until the last step loses those buyers to a marketplace listing.",
      "<strong>Payments.</strong> Card payments remain essential, and PayNow has become an everyday way to pay: buyers scan an SGQR code or approve a transfer in their banking app, and the money reaches your business account through your UEN. Stripe supports cards, Apple Pay, Google Pay, PayNow and GrabPay for Singapore merchants in a single integration, which is why we often recommend it for custom stores. Shopify stores can use Shopify Payments for cards and wallets and add other methods through apps. Local gateways such as HitPay are popular with smaller merchants and market stalls that also sell in person. Fees, settlement times and supported methods change, so we check the current terms with you before choosing. Every merchant account is opened in your company's name, never ours.",
      "<strong>Buy now, pay later.</strong> Instalment options such as Atome can lift conversion for higher-priced items like furniture, electronics and beauty treatments. They also add fees and a layer of customer-service questions, so we suggest adding them only where average order values justify it and only after the core checkout is reliable.",
      "<strong>Platform choice.</strong> Shopify suits most small and mid-sized retailers: hosting, security, PCI compliance for payments and upgrades are handled for you, and staff can learn the admin in an afternoon. WooCommerce suits businesses that already run WordPress and want lower monthly platform costs and full control of their data. A custom build on a headless setup suits unusual cases: B2B price lists per customer, complex bundles, booking and retail in one flow, or catalogues that need to sync with an existing ERP. We will tell you which one fits, including when the answer is simply a well-configured Shopify store.",
      "<strong>Delivery and self-collection.</strong> Singapore stores typically offer standard delivery, express or same-day delivery for a fee, and self-collection from the shop or a pickup locker network. We configure shipping zones and rates, delivery date and time-slot selection where you need it, and connect the store to your courier or delivery platform so orders and tracking links flow automatically. Free-delivery thresholds are worth testing: a clear threshold shown in the cart often raises average order value more than a discount code.",
