      "We quote Singapore clients in US dollars, using the starting prices shown on this page. If your finance team prefers Singapore dollars, we can issue the invoice in SGD at a rate agreed in the quote, so the amount is fixed before work starts. Payment is by Wise or international bank wire. Wise is usually the cheaper and faster option for transfers from Singapore bank accounts, with fees and exchange rates shown before you send.",
      "Payments are staged against visible milestones rather than taken in full upfront. A typical structure is a part advance to start, a part when the design is approved, and the balance before launch, with the exact split written into the quote. Monthly SEO and maintenance plans are billed monthly and can be stopped with notice; the five free months of maintenance after launch cost nothing and do not lock you into a paid plan.",
      "Third-party costs are paid by you directly to the provider: domain registration and renewal, hosting or cloud usage, Shopify or other platform subscriptions, paid themes and plugins, email services, and payment gateway fees. We list the expected running costs in the quote so your total cost of ownership is clear from the start. Keeping these accounts in your company's name is also what guarantees you own everything.",
